# TypeScript conventions

- Strict TS, Node >= 20, ESM. Follow `eslint.config.js`.
- Cross-platform rules (non-negotiable, CONTRIBUTING.md): `node:path` for every path, never
  string-concatenate; `spawn`/`execFile` with argv arrays and `shell: false`; no native addons —
  pure JS/TS deps only; preserve a file's existing line endings on write
  (`src/util/lineEndings.ts`); `os.tmpdir()`, never `/tmp`.
- No new dependency without asking — this is a globally-installed CLI, the dependency tree matters.
- Vitest tests in `test/<subject>.test.ts` — happy path + edge case; a safety-invariant change
  needs an explicit regression test.
- No new NuGet/npm packages, no direct DB/network calls outside `src/integrations/` and `src/llm/`.
